  "geometryBasis": "OpenStreetMap way 406667535 and its four independently measured corner coordinates. Preserve the mapped axes and leave the historic interior open.",
  "sectionBasis": "The measured wall lower section consists of battered rammed earth with mudbrick above. Use the recurring eroded rounded embankments and openings in the cleared southwestern view, with original elevation profiles on all four walls.",
  "limitations": [
    "The current mapped corners register the complete enclosure within several metres at map scale. Individual crest positions, elevation changes, width of eroded breaches and tower remnants are estimated.",
    "Ninara’s southwestern view covers one part of the wall. The remaining sides and the damaged gate sectors use archaeological descriptions, road crossings and the original relief. Present heights away from the photo remain approximate.",
    "The terrain remains an unmodified Terrarium composite, including its low-resolution signal from the rampart. The wall uses nearby terrain samples for its base. Only the surviving circuit and open interior are represented."
